/* ============================================================================
   LabRef — Laboratory Test Reference
   DATA MODULE  v2.0
   ----------------------------------------------------------------------------
   This file holds the entire content database. The UI reads from it and never
   writes to it. To extend the app, append records to LABREF_TESTS following the
   schema documented in the handover package's SCHEMA.md. Do not change field names.

   SCHEMA SUMMARY (full spec + worked examples in SCHEMA.md)
   id            unique slug, lowercase, hyphenated
   name          full display name
   abbr          short form shown in list rows
   syn[]         search synonyms (Indian usage included: KFT, LFT, TLC...)
   cat           category id from LABREF_CATEGORIES
   specimen      specimen type text
   tube          { id, vol, handling } — id refers to LABREF_TUBES
   prep          { fasting, items[], patient[] }
                 items[]   = instructions for the CLINICIAN / collection staff
                 patient[] = plain-language instructions for the PATIENT handout.
                             Omit when the patient need do nothing special.
   assayDep      true when the cutoff is analyser-specific
   units         { conv, si, factor }   si_value = conv_value * factor.
                 This is a PANEL-LEVEL DEFAULT only. A test that bundles more than
                 one real analyte (a panel) MUST NOT be assumed to convert every
                 row at this one factor — see ranges[].analyte below.
   ranges[]      { grp, analyte, sex, age, preg, conv:{lo,hi,txt}, si:{lo,hi,txt} }
                 lo/hi null = open-ended; txt overrides numeric display
                 analyte (OPTIONAL) = {key, label, factor?, noConvert?}
                 Set this when a test record bundles more than one real,
                 separately-reported analyte or assay family under one id —
                 e.g. Lipid Profile (total/LDL/HDL/triglycerides/non-HDL),
                 ABG Panel (pH/PaCO2/PaO2/HCO3/base excess/SaO2/anion gap),
                 PT/INR (PT in seconds vs INR, a unitless ratio), Troponin
                 (hs-cTnI vs hs-cTnT are different assays — a lab reports one,
                 never both), Bilirubin (total vs direct), Calcium (total vs
                 ionised). Rows that share the same analyte.key are the SAME
                 component shown under different patient-mode conditions (e.g.
                 "LDL-C — optimal" and "LDL-C — very high CV risk target" are
                 both key:"ldl"); rows with different keys are genuinely
                 different measurements and must never be cross-matched,
                 cross-converted, or collapsed into one "best range" or one
                 My Lab override box. key = short stable id, label = display
                 name for the component's own sub-section and override block.
                 factor, if the component's own mg/dL<->SI (or equivalent)
                 conversion differs from the test's panel-level units.factor,
                 e.g. triglycerides converts at 0.0113 while the Lipid Profile
                 panel default (cholesterol species) is 0.0259 — getting this
                 wrong silently mis-converts the displayed SI value. noConvert:
                 true when the component has no meaningful second unit (pH,
                 SaO2, qualitative results) — suppresses the conversion
                 footnote for that component rather than showing a wrong one.
                 Omit analyte entirely for an ordinary single-analyte test;
                 the UI falls back to one range table and one override box.
   critical      { txt, lo, hi, analyte? }  (null when not a critical-value
                 test). analyte (OPTIONAL, panel tests only) = [key, key, …]
                 — restricts this critical value to the named component(s)
                 only, e.g. Lipid Profile's "Triglycerides >1000 mg/dL" is
                 analyte:["trig"], and Calcium's/Bilirubin's single critical
                 figure is analyte:["total"] (it does not describe ionised
                 calcium or direct bilirubin). Omit analyte when the critical
                 value is genuinely test-wide (Troponin: the same 99th-
                 percentile logic applies whichever assay is in use) or
                 already names its own components inline (ABG Panel, PT/INR).
                 The Result Interpreter only shows a panel test's critical
                 value when analyte is absent or includes the selected
                 component's key, so a value for one analyte is never shown
                 while interpreting a different one.
   inc[]         causes of raised value
   dec[]         causes of low value
   interf[]      analytical interferences
   pearls[]      interpretation notes
   rel[]         related test ids

   LABREF_TUBES[] entry fields: id, order (CLSI draw position, 0 if not
   applicable), name, colors (full cap-colour description — may be prose,
   not just a colour, e.g. blood culture bottles are brand-specific and not
   CLSI colour-coded), shortColor (optional — short label for compact UI
   rows; falls back to colors when absent), additive, inv, uses, notes.
   ============================================================================ */

