  pearls:["Corrected Ca (mg/dL) = measured Ca + 0.8 × (4.0 − albumin g/dL). In SI: corrected Ca (mmol/L) = measured + 0.02 × (40 − albumin g/L).","Correction formulae are unreliable in critical illness — measure ionised calcium when it matters.","Chvostek and Trousseau signs appear with acute falls; chronic hypocalcaemia may be asymptomatic at the same level.","Hypercalcaemia with a non-suppressed PTH is hyperparathyroidism; with a suppressed PTH, look for malignancy or granulomatous disease."],
