      items:["Always send a concurrent FBC and ferritin. Iron deficiency LOWERS HbA2 and can mask beta-thalassaemia trait — correct the iron deficiency and repeat if the clinical suspicion is high.","Record any transfusion in the previous 3 months; transfused donor cells make the pattern uninterpretable.","Record ethnicity and family history, and state if this is a premarital or antenatal screen."],
