    dec:["Not clinically significant."],
    interf:["Even trace heparin from a flushed line markedly prolongs the thrombin time."],
    pearls:["Thrombin time's main use is as a heparin detector. A prolonged APTT with a prolonged TT and a normal reptilase time means heparin.","It is exquisitely sensitive to dabigatran — a NORMAL thrombin time effectively excludes clinically significant dabigatran levels, which is useful before urgent surgery or thrombolysis.","A prolonged TT with a normal fibrinogen points to dysfibrinogenaemia or a thrombin inhibitor rather than a quantity problem.","Always ask where the sample was drawn from before investigating further."],
