    pearls:["Free T4 has largely replaced total T4 precisely because total T4 tracks binding proteins. A pregnant woman typically has a total T4 about 1.5 times non-pregnant levels and is perfectly euthyroid.","Total T4 still has a role where free hormone assays are unreliable or unavailable, and in some assay-interference situations.","If the TSH and the total T4 disagree, trust the TSH in the outpatient setting and look for a binding-protein explanation.","In India this test is still commonly reported in thyroid profiles alongside T3 and TSH — interpret it as a binding-protein-dependent number, not a direct measure of thyroid function."],
