    inc:["Hyperthyroidism, including T3 toxicosis","Raised TBG: pregnancy, oestrogen, the combined oral contraceptive","Liothyronine therapy"],
    dec:["Non-thyroidal illness — the commonest reason for a low T3 in hospital","Hypothyroidism (a late change)","Reduced TBG states; amiodarone, propranolol, steroids","Starvation"],
    interf:["Binding-protein changes move total T3 without any change in thyroid status.","Biotin interference on immunoassay platforms."],
    pearls:["A low total T3 in an unwell inpatient almost always means non-thyroidal illness, not hypothyroidism. Resist the temptation to treat it.","T3 toxicosis is the specific indication: clinical thyrotoxicosis with a suppressed TSH and a normal FT4 — check a T3.","T3 is not useful for diagnosing or monitoring hypothyroidism; TSH and FT4 do that job.","Indian thyroid profiles frequently report T3, T4 and TSH together. Base decisions on TSH first, FT4 second, and treat T3 as supplementary."],
