    inc:["Primary gonadal failure — premature ovarian insufficiency, Klinefelter syndrome, orchitis, chemotherapy","Menopause","Polycystic ovary syndrome — LH often raised with a raised LH:FSH ratio","Mid-cycle physiological surge","Precocious puberty (central)"],
    dec:["Hypogonadotropic hypogonadism — pituitary or hypothalamic disease, Kallmann syndrome","Hyperprolactinaemia suppressing GnRH","Functional hypothalamic amenorrhoea: weight loss, excessive exercise, stress","Hormonal contraception, GnRH analogues, anabolic steroid use","Constitutional delay of puberty"],
    interf:["Biotin interference on immunoassay platforms.","hCG cross-reacts with LH in some older assays — pregnancy can produce a spuriously high LH."],
    pearls:["LH and FSH must be read together, and against oestradiol or testosterone. The pattern tells you the level of the problem: both high with low sex steroid is primary gonadal failure; both low or inappropriately normal with low sex steroid is pituitary or hypothalamic.","An LH:FSH ratio above about 2:1 supports PCOS but is neither sensitive nor specific — PCOS is diagnosed on the Rotterdam criteria, not on this ratio.","In a woman with amenorrhoea, always check prolactin and thyroid function alongside; both cause secondary amenorrhoea and are reversible.","In prepubertal children, standard adult assays lack the sensitivity to distinguish low from very low — a specialist ultrasensitive assay and GnRH stimulation testing are needed to assess precocious puberty."],
