    dec:["Hypogonadotropic hypogonadism (pituitary or hypothalamic)","Hyperprolactinaemia","Functional hypothalamic amenorrhoea","Hormonal contraception, GnRH analogues, anabolic steroids","Constitutional delay of puberty"],
    interf:["Biotin interference on immunoassay platforms.","Heterophile antibodies can cause falsely high results."],
    pearls:["A raised day 2–5 FSH indicates reduced ovarian reserve, but AMH is more reliable because it can be measured on any day of the cycle and is less variable.","Do not diagnose menopause biochemically in a woman over 45 with typical symptoms and absent periods — it is a clinical diagnosis. FSH is for atypical cases and for women under 45.","FSH cannot be interpreted while a woman is on combined hormonal contraception; stop it for at least six weeks first.","In male infertility, a raised FSH with small testes suggests primary testicular failure and a poor prognosis for sperm retrieval; a normal FSH with azoospermia suggests obstruction, which is potentially correctable."],
