    inc:["Ovarian stimulation during IVF — monitored to avoid ovarian hyperstimulation syndrome","Pregnancy","Oestrogen-secreting tumours (granulosa cell tumour)","Gynaecomastia in men: testicular tumour, liver disease, obesity (peripheral aromatisation)","Exogenous oestrogen, including topical preparations"],
    dec:["Menopause and premature ovarian insufficiency","Hypogonadotropic hypogonadism","Functional hypothalamic amenorrhoea: low weight, excessive exercise, stress","Turner syndrome","Aromatase inhibitors"],
    interf:["Standard immunoassays are unreliable at the very low concentrations found in post-menopausal women, men and children — LC-MS/MS is required for these groups.","Biotin interference on immunoassay platforms."],
    pearls:["The single most important limitation: routine immunoassays are not accurate at low oestradiol levels. If you need an accurate value in a child, a man or a post-menopausal woman, request a mass spectrometry assay.","In suspected precocious or delayed puberty, send to a specialist laboratory — ordinary assays cannot reliably distinguish prepubertal from early pubertal levels.","Read oestradiol with LH and FSH. Low oestradiol with high gonadotropins is ovarian failure; low with low or normal gonadotropins points to the pituitary or hypothalamus.","During IVF stimulation, a rapidly rising oestradiol with many follicles warns of ovarian hyperstimulation syndrome."],
