    prep:{ fasting:"Not required",
      items:["Avoid NSAIDs for at least 2–4 weeks before testing where clinically possible — they raise calprotectin and cause false positives.","Avoid testing during or soon after an episode of infective gastroenteritis, which also raises it.","Not useful in the presence of frank rectal bleeding or an obvious alternative diagnosis."],
      patient:["Avoid painkillers such as ibuprofen or diclofenac for two to four weeks before this test if you can — ask the doctor first.","Wait until any stomach bug has fully settled before giving the sample."] },
